        Efficient global <span class="search-hit mathjax">optimization</span> is the problem of minimizing an unknown function f, using as few evaluations f(x) as possible. It can be considered as a continuum-armed bandit problem, with noiseless data and simple regret. Expected improvement is perhaps the most popular method for solving this problem; the algorithm performs well in experiments, but little i&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('1101.3501v3-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('1101.3501v3-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
